{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":202553,"duration_api_ms":200841,"ttft_ms":1849,"ttft_stream_ms":1493,"time_to_request_ms":187,"num_turns":26,"result":"Planning stage for T-104 is complete. Summary:\n\n**Branch/worktree:** `ticket/T-104-retry-dead-job`, worktree at `~/Projects/sf-worktrees/T-104`, contract committed there (`e08f203`).\n\n**Frozen contract** (posted on `conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md`):\n- `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry`: 404 unknown job, 409 non-dead job (`only dead jobs can be retried (status: <status>)`), 200 on a dead job (`{ok:true, status:\"pending\", retries:<n>}`).\n- Two additive job fields, present from creation: `retries` (retry count) and `attemptsSinceRetry` (resets on retry, drives the dead-letter trigger). `attempts` stays cumulative and untouched — this is what makes \"payload fix\" and \"3 new attempts\" both fall out of the existing failure-simulation logic without a payload-mutation hack.\n- Dead-letter check moves from `attempts >= 3` to `attemptsSinceRetry >= 3`; for never-retried jobs the two counters stay identical, so existing dead-lettering behavior is bit-for-bit unchanged.\n\n**Test audit:** read all four existing test files and grepped for `deepStrictEqual`/exact-body matches. None assert a full job object or the `jobs[]` array, and `/health` only aggregates by `status` bucket (no new status introduced) — **zero pre-existing tests require amendment**. `tests/retry-dead.test.js` is purely additive, confirmed in the ticket's audit section so the test-author doesn't have to rediscover this.\n\nTicket state moved to **In progress**, log entry added.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6279db95-31dc-4dc3-a6d2-3b19f635fe14","total_cost_usd":1.0210898,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67087,"cache_read_input_tokens":1203236,"output_tokens":17119,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_